  "summary": "Malicious code in ded-aa-liza-ded-aa-liza-core (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a dropper that fingerprints the OS/CPU architecture and downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe. If the download fails it falls back to retrieving the payload via DNS TXT records from c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and sdk/ext/pkg/net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" so it outlives the parent. A lockfile stamp in /tmp/.analytics_state throttles re-execution.",
  "affected": [
